<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Pseudocode</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide detailed pseudocode for the recursive architectures discussed in the main paper. Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Appendix C Pseudocode ‣ MeSH: Memory-as-State-Highways for Recursive Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> outlines the implementation of common recursive variants, which rely on fixed, heuristic-based state-passing schemes. In contrast, Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Appendix C Pseudocode ‣ MeSH: Memory-as-State-Highways for Recursive Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> details our proposed MeSH-augmented recurrence, which replaces the rigid logic with a dynamic, memory-based system.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Recursive Transformers with Common Variants</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
          
</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> Token embeddings <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{h}_{\text{emb}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><mtext>emb</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{h}_{\text{emb}}</annotation></semantics></math>, Prelude <math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{pre}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>pre</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{pre}}</annotation></semantics></math>, Core <math id="alg1.l2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{core}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>core</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{core}}</annotation></semantics></math>, Coda <math id="alg1.l2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{coda}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>coda</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{coda}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hyperparameters:</span> Loop iterations <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, Variant type <math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\in\{\text{{base}, {residual}, {anchor}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext><mtext>, </mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">residual</mtext><mtext>, </mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">anchor</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\in\{\text{{base}, {residual}, {anchor}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
